From 768972909e9843a32cbae0105fff459e0ef276ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:12:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/42] amdgpu: untrack the LGKM record when an icache
 invalidate has no lanes

Inst_SOPP__S_ICACHE_INV decremented the LGKM counter on the empty execution
mask path but left its entry in the issued-instruction record, unlike every
other memory instruction. The stale entry produced a spurious "not in LGKM
issued" warning when the record was later retired.

This affects the diagnostic record only; the wait counter itself was already
balanced, so no wait condition changes. The warning only became visible after
the periodic progress report was enabled, because the record is not maintained
when that report is disabled.

Checkpoint-ID: CP-0032
Goal-ID: GSIM-001
Plan-Revision: 15
Source-Lock-SHA256: 8c0a6d1d04d5a73ab036ddc56d09ff59f7513077931868bdfac5a763f85a73d4
Evidence-Manifest-SHA256: 458368899b9122d48baf6268c84e035737cdb2e36776c5b374a26b176ed5df69
Change-Kind: code
Baseline-Commit: 9df727743024f9f0cc83d2b9ef23e03b632cc513
---
 src/arch/amdgpu/vega/insts/sopp.cc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/arch/amdgpu/vega/insts/sopp.cc b/src/arch/amdgpu/vega/insts/sopp.cc
index 781113b20..6c0339ccd 100644
--- a/src/arch/amdgpu/vega/insts/sopp.cc
+++ b/src/arch/amdgpu/vega/insts/sopp.cc
@@ -690,6 +690,7 @@ namespace VegaISA
 
         if (gpuDynInst->exec_mask.none()) {
             wf->decLGKMInstsIssued();
+            wf->untrackLGKMInst(gpuDynInst);
             return;
         }
 
